/Pg 9 0 R
/K [1 2]
>>
endobj
118 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The Dynamic Programing \(DP\) method uses the Bellman equation to compute the value of a state, allowing for bootstrapping. This means that the value of a state can be estimated based on the value of the next state, rather than waiting until the end of the episode.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [3]
>>
